            <ArticleTitle>Flexible method for fabricating protein patterns on superhydrophobic platforms controlled by magnetic field.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>408-411</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6bm00867d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inspired by the rolling of water droplets on lotus leaves, we developed a novel, magnetic field-controlled patterning method for water-soluble proteins and other functional materials on superhydrophobic platforms. This simple method can be used to fabricate biochips and open micro-fluidic devices in a simple way.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
